title: Party Disunity
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: party_disunity_timer = 0 and (dissent >= 0.3 or insurgent_dissent > 30 or progressive_dissent > 30 or labor_left_dissent > 30 or blue_dog_dissent > 30)
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; party_disunity_timer = 4
card-image: img/Reichstagsfraktion_der_SPD.jpg
frequency: 200
tags: party_affairs

= Party Disunity

The coalition is being pulled apart by internal dissent. Frustrated with leadership and general direction, factions have started working against each other, hampering our ability to win elections and pass legislation.

[? if insurgent_dissent > 30 and not insurgent_split : The insurgent wing is making real noise about running independently. ?]
[? if progressive_dissent > 30 and not progressive_split : The progressive wing is deeply unhappy with our present direction. ?]
[? if labor_left_dissent > 30 and not labor_left_split : Organized labor is losing patience with the coalition. ?]
[? if blue_dog_dissent > 30 and not blue_dog_split : The blue-dog wing is questioning whether it's worth staying. ?]

Something must be done to hold the coalition together - or a faction may decide it isn't worth staying.

- @enforce_unity
- @concessions_insurgent
- @concessions_progressive
- @concessions_labor_left
- @concessions_blue_dog
- @do_nothing


@enforce_unity
title: Enforce coalition discipline.
on-arrival: insurgent_dissent -= 5; progressive_dissent -= 5; labor_left_dissent -= 5; blue_dog_dissent -= 5; establishment_dem_dissent -= 5; working_class_dem -= 4; college_educated_dem -= 2; suburban_dem -= 2
go-to: check_splits

Enforcing coalition discipline reduces dissent across the board, but risks alienating members who feel unheard.

@concessions_insurgent
title: Give ground to the insurgent wing.
view-if: insurgent_dissent > 30 and not insurgent_split
on-arrival: insurgent_dissent -= 8; establishment_dem_dissent += 5; blue_dog_dissent += 3
go-to: check_splits

We commit to giving the insurgent wing a real seat at the table. This may alienate the establishment and blue-dog wings, however.

@concessions_progressive
title: Give ground to the progressive wing.
view-if: progressive_dissent > 30 and not progressive_split
on-arrival: progressive_dissent -= 8; establishment_dem_dissent += 3; blue_dog_dissent += 2
go-to: check_splits

We commit to taking more policy direction from the progressive wing. The establishment and blue-dog wings may be displeased.

@concessions_labor_left
title: Give ground to organized labor.
view-if: labor_left_dissent > 30 and not labor_left_split
on-arrival: labor_left_dissent -= 8; establishment_dem_dissent += 4
go-to: check_splits

Organized labor will be granted more influence over coalition strategy. This upsets the establishment wing, which would prefer to keep decision-making centralized.

@concessions_blue_dog
title: Give ground to the blue-dog wing.
view-if: blue_dog_dissent > 30 and not blue_dog_split
on-arrival: blue_dog_dissent -= 8; insurgent_dissent += 6; progressive_dissent += 4
go-to: check_splits

We commit to giving frontline members more room to break with the coalition on votes that threaten their seats. This infuriates the insurgent and progressive wings.

@do_nothing
title: Let the factions argue among themselves.
on-arrival: insurgent_dissent += 1; progressive_dissent += 1; labor_left_dissent += 1; blue_dog_dissent += 1
go-to: check_splits

Let the factions bicker; perhaps a little internal argument is healthy. But left unaddressed for too long, it won't stay healthy.

@check_splits
on-arrival: {!
// ==========================================================
// GENERALIZED FACTION-SPLIT TRIGGER
// Any splittable faction (insurgent, progressive, labor_left, blue_dog -
// everyone except establishment_dem, which defines "the party as it is")
// can break off to run independently once its dissent has stayed above
// split_dissent_threshold. This generalizes the original's single scripted
// SPD/SAPD split into a repeatable system, per design decision.
// ==========================================================
Q.faction_that_split = null;
for (var f of Q.splittable_factions) {
    if (Q[f + '_split'] === 1) {
        continue; // already split, nothing to do
    }
    if (Q[f + '_dissent'] > Q.split_dissent_threshold) {
        Q.faction_that_split = f;
        break; // only one faction can split per visit to this card
    }
}
!}
go-to: do_split if faction_that_split != null; no_split if faction_that_split == null

@no_split

For now, the coalition holds - barely.

@do_split
on-arrival: {!
var f = Q.faction_that_split;
Q[f + '_split'] = 1;

// name the breakaway organization
var splitNames = {
    insurgent: "the Working Families Alliance",
    progressive: "the Progressive Alliance",
    labor_left: "the Labor Party",
    blue_dog: "the New Democrats"
};
Q[f + '_split_name'] = splitNames[f] || (f + " (independent)");

var factionLabels = {
    insurgent: "The insurgent wing",
    progressive: "The progressive wing",
    labor_left: "The labor-left wing",
    blue_dog: "The blue-dog wing"
};
Q.faction_that_split_label = factionLabels[f] || f;

// add the breakaway as a new line in the general-election party list,
// siphoning initial demographic support away from 'dem' proportional to
// the splitting faction's overall strength relative to the coalition.
var newParty = f + '_split_party';
Q.parties.push(newParty);
var shareOfCoalition = Q[f + '_strength'] / (Q.insurgent_strength + Q.progressive_strength + Q.labor_left_strength + Q.establishment_dem_strength + Q.blue_dog_strength);
for (var c of Q.classes) {
    var siphoned = Q[c + '_dem'] * shareOfCoalition * 0.6;
    Q[c + '_dem'] -= siphoned;
    Q[c + '_' + newParty] = siphoned;
}

// backfill historical records so charts don't break
for (var record of Q.election_records) {
    record[newParty] = 0;
}
for (var record of Q.party_support_records) {
    record[newParty] = 0;
}

// the remaining coalition's dissent drops with the departure, but trust
// is damaged
Q[f + '_dissent'] = 0;
Q.dissent += 0.05;
Q.establishment_dem_dissent -= 5;
Q.split_announcement = Q[f + '_split_name'];
!}

[+ faction_that_split_label +] has formally broken from the coalition, forming [+ split_announcement +] to run independently. They will no longer contest the Democratic primary, and will instead appear as their own line on the general election ballot.

This is a serious blow to coalition unity, though it may also relieve some of the internal pressure that led here.

- @return: Continue...
